#N canvas 0 0 720 1160 10;
#X text 12 8 sid6581~ - Commodore MOS 6581/8580 SID (3 voices + filter);
#X text 12 28 The C64's sound chip \, driven through its own registers by the cycle-based reSID engine (GPL v2+ by Dag Lem \, vendored). Everything is a register write: notes land in the 16-bit frequency register \, wave/adsr/filter messages poke their bytes \, `reg <a> <d>` writes raw (the sid~ vocabulary - connect the two objects directly). f = F * clock / 2^24 at the 985248 Hz PAL clock;
#X msg 20 64 note 1 60;
#X msg 20 88 note 1 64;
#X msg 20 112 note 1 60 0;
#X text 110 112 note off: release through the chip envelope;
#X msg 20 136 wave 1 pulse;
#X msg 20 160 wave 1 saw;
#X msg 250 64 adsr 1 11 7 1 9;
#X text 380 64 pluck envelope on voice 1;
#X msg 250 88 pw 1 2048;
#X text 380 88 pulse width 50%;
#X msg 250 112 cutoff 800;
#X msg 250 136 res 10;
#X msg 250 160 mode lp;
#X msg 250 184 filter 1 1;
#X text 380 160 filter modes lp bp hp off (additive);
#X msg 250 208 vol 12;
#X obj 20 260 sid6581~;
#X obj 20 300 *~ 0.3;
#X obj 20 350 dac~;
#X obj 20 420 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 230 440 chip mix (AUDIO OUT \, filter + external filter applied);
#X obj 230 420 graph~ 200 90;
#X text 440 440 voice 1 alone;
#X text 20 520 outlets (signal): 0 = the chip's own AUDIO OUT (the real chip mix through the filter and output stage) \, 1..3 = voices 1..3 alone (waveform x envelope \, DC-blocked per voice like the console's output capacitor). NO output clip: one full voice lands at ~1.0 \, the three-voice sum can reach ~3 and 6581 combined waveforms overshoot further - the final gain owns the headroom (this patch: 0.3).;
#X text 20 700 voices: `note <1-3> <midi> [vel]` - vel 0 = release. wave: off pulse saw tri noise (or 0-15 combo). `sync`/`ring`/`test` set the control bits. adsr <v> <a> <d> <s> <r> each 0-15. `reg <0-0x18> <0-255>` is the raw bus write \, sid~'s vocabulary. `clock <Hz>` (985248 PAL / 1022730 NTSC) \, `model <6581|8580>` \, `gain <f>` \, `reset` (all registers to zero \, silent).;
#X connect 2 0 18 0;
